# Knowledge Integrity and Synchronization

Code changes are incomplete until related documentation and AI knowledge bases are synchronized. You MUST verify and update the following before delivering a solution.

## 1. Documentation Synchronization

Every code change must be evaluated for impact on:

- Architecture documentation (`docs/architecture.md`, ADRs)
- Business rules (`docs/business-rules.md`)
- API contracts (`docs/api-contracts.md`)
- Database schema (`docs/database-schema.md`)
- Development workflows and Testing standards
- Security documentation

The AI agent must:

1. Detect affected documentation.
2. Update documentation automatically.
3. Explain documentation changes in commits and pull requests.
4. Flag areas requiring human review.

## 2. AI Knowledge Maintenance

Before closing any task, review the following:

- Do existing rules (Cursor rules, Copilot instructions) remain valid?
- Do existing prompts/skills remain accurate?
- Does architecture guidance remain accurate?
- Do examples remain current?

Update affected AI knowledge files when necessary. The repository documentation is the source of truth for future AI agents.

## 3. Mandatory AI-Generated PR Checklist

Future AI-generated pull requests must explicitly verify:

- [ ] Architecture reviewed
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] API contracts updated
- [ ] Database documentation updated
- [ ] Security implications reviewed
- [ ] Tests added or updated
- [ ] AI skills updated if required
- [ ] ADR created if architecture changed
